howtoplay.aoc.introduction.h4=Generators
howtoplay.aoc.introduction.p1=§bAdvance Chemistry§r is a chemistry and industrial addon built as an expansion of §6UtilityCraft§r.\n\nAll machines run on §eDE (Dorios Energy)§r — the shared energy system from UtilityCraft.\n\nThis addon was created by Rudransh (developer) and MasterAtib (texture designer).
howtoplay.aoc.introduction.p2=The main processing flow:\n\n§b1.§r §aDissolution Chamber§r — converts organic inputs into §ePlant Oil§r, §aEthanol§r, or §2Organic Fertilizer§r\n§b2.§r §6Fluid Mixer§r — combines §aEthanol§r and §aPlant Oil§r into §6Biofuel§r\n§b3.§r §dChemical Reactor§r — processes fluids into §dHydrocarbon Slurry§r, §7Crude Oil§r, or §3Plastic Resin§r\n§b4.§r §bSeparator§r — separates §8Hydrocarbon Slurry§r into §7Heavy Hydrocarbon§r and §dReactive Fluid§r\n§b5.§r §cRefinery§r — processes §7Crude Oil§r into §cDiesel§r, §6Petrol§r, and §7Naphtha§r\n§b6.§r §3Polymerizer§r — converts §3Plastic Resin§r into §3HDPE Pellets§r
howtoplay.aoc.introduction.p3=§eDE (Dorios Energy)§r is produced by the §bIndustrial Generators§r included in this addon.\n\nFluids are moved between machines using §bFluid Valves§r. Each machine has a §7fluid tank§r shown in its UI.\n\nUse the §7IO tab§r in each machine's UI to configure which face accepts inputs and which exports outputs — enabling full pipe and hopper automation.
howtoplay.aoc.introduction.p4=Every machine has an §bIO tab§r. Switch to it and assign each face:\n\n§a● Input§r — accepts items or fluids\n§c● Output§r — exports items or fluids\n§7● Disabled§r — blocks all transfer\n\nThe §eUpgrades tab§r lets you insert §aSpeed§r and §bEnergy§r upgrade modules to improve throughput.
howtoplay.aoc.introduction.p5=Industrial generators produce §eDE§r to power all machines. Choose based on your available fuel:\n\n§7Furnator§r — burns solid fuel (coal, wood). Best early-game.\n§7Magmator§r — burns lava. Mid-game power.\n§7Solar Panel§r — passive sunlight power. Zero fuel cost.\n§7Thermo Generator§r — hot + cold fluid differential. High output.\n§7Wind Turbine§r — passive wind power. Higher placement = more output.
