howtoplay.aoc.multiblock.intro=Multiblock machines are large structures made of §bcasings§r controlled by a §bmonitor§r or §bcontroller§r. Right-click the monitor/controller with a §eWrench§r to activate. Pipe fluids and energy through §bFluid Valves§r and §bEnergy Valves§r.
howtoplay.aoc.multiblock.p_fluid_storage=Large-capacity multiblock tank for storing up to §b7 independent fluid types§r simultaneously.\n\n§aCapacity:§r Scales with structure size\n§lTanks:§r Tanks 1–7, each independently accessible\n\n§lStructure:§r Fluid Storage Casings + Fluid Storage Monitor\n§7IO:§r Each Fluid Valve on the monitor can target Any Tank or a specific tank (1–7). Both input and output are supported on every tank.\n\n§7Use Fluid Valves to pipe fluids in and out. Right-click a valve with a Wrench to filter by fluid type.
howtoplay.aoc.multiblock.p_fuel_burner=Burns §bfluid fuels§r to generate large amounts of §eDE§r.\n\n§cAccepted fuels:§r Biofuel, Diesel, Petrol\n§aOutput:§r High DE generation\n\n§lStructure:§r Fuel Burner Casings + Fuel Burner Monitor\n§7Activate:§r Right-click monitor with Wrench\n§7IO:§r Fluid valve for fuel input, Energy valve for DE export.
howtoplay.aoc.multiblock.p_fusion_reactor=Burns §bliquid fuels§r at high temperature to generate §eDE§r. Requires continuous fuel, coolant supply, and exhaust drainage.\n\n§lSupported fuels:§r Biofuel, Ethanol, Diesel, Heavy Hydrocarbon, Fissile Fuel\n§7Higher-tier fuels produce far more DE per bucket but run much hotter.\n\n§lCoolants:§r Water, Saline Coolant, Liquid Nitrogen\n§7Insufficient coolant reduces efficiency and raises temperature.\n\n§lExhaust:§r Reactive Fluid produced each cycle. Drain via Fluid Ports.\n§7A full exhaust tank pauses the reactor — keep it flowing.\n\n§lFuel tiers:§r\n  §aBiofuel / Ethanol§r — low tier, clean and renewable\n  §cHeavy Hydrocarbon / Fissile Fuel§r — high tier, extreme heat, use Liquid Nitrogen
howtoplay.aoc.multiblock.p_greenhouse=A §b5×5×5§r industrial crop processor that grows up to §b4 seed types simultaneously§r.\n\n§lStructure:§r\n§7Outer shell:§r Industrial Casing + Industrial Ports\n§7Interior:§r hollow (growing chamber)\n§7Controller:§r Greenhouse Controller\n\n§lRequired ports:§r\n§e1× Industrial Energy Port§r — powers the machine\n§92× Industrial Fluid Ports§r — fertilizer + growth solution input\n§a1× Industrial Item Port§r — harvest output\n\n§lFertilizers §7(optional):§r\n  Organic — ×1.10 yield, 100 mB/cycle\n  Enriched — ×1.25 yield, 80 mB/cycle\n  Industrial — ×1.50 yield, 60 mB/cycle\n\n§lGrowth Solutions §7(optional):§r\n  Bio — ×1.20 speed, 100 mB/cycle\n  Nutrient — ×1.40 speed, 80 mB/cycle\n  Advanced Catalyst — ×1.70 speed, 60 mB/cycle\n\n§lSoil types:§r\n§fDirt§r — base  §aYellow§r — ×1.0 yield  §cRed§r — ×2.0  §9Blue§r — ×3.0  §8Black§r — ×4.0\n\n§7Output halts when all 9 harvest slots are full.
howtoplay.aoc.multiblock.p_ind_ports=Exclusive connection points for the §bIndustrial Greenhouse§r and §bNuclear Reactor§r multiblocks. They replace standard valves for these structures.\n\n§eIndustrial Energy Port§r — accepts or exports §eDE§r\n§9Industrial Fluid Port§r — inputs or outputs fluids; use a §eWrench§r to configure which tank each port targets\n§aIndustrial Item Port§r — exports harvested crops from the 9 output slots\n\n§7Standard fluid valves and energy valves are §cnot§r accepted by these multiblocks.
howtoplay.aoc.multiblock.p_nuclear_reactor=§c3×3×3§r nuclear fission reactor. Consumes §eLiquified Thorium§r and a §bcoolant§r to produce §eDE§r, with §2Nuclear Waste§r as a byproduct.\n\n§lCoolants:§r\n  §fWater§r — ×1.0 speed, 150 mB/cycle\n  §bSaline Coolant§r — ×1.5 speed, 100 mB/cycle\n  §3Liquid Nitrogen§r — ×2.0 speed, 60 mB/cycle\n  §7No coolant§r — ×0.5 speed\n\n§lPer cycle:§r\n  §cThorium:§r 50 mB consumed\n  §eDE:§r 50 000 produced\n  §2Waste:§r 10 mB produced\n\n§lStructure:§r 3×3×3 Industrial Casing + Nuclear Reactor Controller\n§lPorts:§r §92× Industrial Fluid Port§r (thorium in, waste out), §e1× Industrial Energy Port§r (DE export)\n§7Throttles automatically at 95%% buffer capacity.
howtoplay.aoc.multiblock.p_refinery=Processes §7Crude Oil§r into multiple refined products simultaneously.\n\n§eDE cost:§r 12 000 per craft\n\n§lRecipe:§r\n§7Crude Oil§r 1 000 mB → §cDiesel§r 350 mB + §6Petrol§r 300 mB + §7Naphtha§r 200 mB\n\n§lStructure:§r Refinery Casings + Refinery Monitor\n§7Activate:§r Right-click monitor with Wrench\n§7IO:§r 1 fluid valve for crude oil input, 3 fluid valves for product outputs, energy valve for DE.
howtoplay.aoc.multiblock.p_stellar_energy_reactor=Burns §bNether Stars§r to generate massive amounts of §eDE§r, with a §d20% chance§r of producing a §fDead Star§r byproduct.\n\n§lStats:§r\n§a5,000,000 DE§r per Nether Star\n§b10-second§r cycle time\n§d20%%§r Dead Star byproduct chance\n§eBuffer:§r 50 MDE\n\n§lStructure:§r 3×3×3 Industrial Casing + Stellar Energy Reactor Controller\n§lPorts:§r §e1× Industrial Energy Port§r (DE export)\n\n§7Input: Nether Stars (left slot). Dead Stars appear in right output slot.
howtoplay.aoc.multiblock.p_valves=§bFluid Valve§r — Controls fluid flow between machines and tanks.\nRight-click to cycle: §aInput§r → §cOutput§r → §7Disabled§r\nUse a §eWrench§r to set a fluid type filter.\n\n§bEnergy Valve§r — Controls §eDE§r flow between generators and machines.\nRight-click to set direction. Wrench to set a transfer rate limit.\n§7Use these to distribute power from generators without overloading connections.
